---
// promptanddone.com/t3code-agents: the AIRFIELD pack (DM deliverable for the "t3code-many-agents-one-app" reel). /go/airfield redirects here.
import PackLayout from '../layouts/PackLayout.astro';
---
<PackLayout title="Run several Claude Code agents at once with T3 Code — Prompt & Done">
  <main>
    <header>
      <p class="kicker"><a href="/">Prompt &amp; Done</a> · AIRFIELD</p>
      <h1>Run three Claude Code agents at once from one free app</h1>
      <p class="tag">T3 Code (pingdotgg/t3code, MIT) is a free, open-source app that runs your coding agents side by side: Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, OpenCode and more, on the logins you already have. Desktop app, local web app, and an iOS / Android app that works as a remote for your computer.</p>
      <p class="note">Checked 7 Nov 2026 against the repo README and docs, and our own run on a Mac (T3 v0.1.7, Claude Code 2.1.319, Claude Sonnet 5.5).</p>
    </header>
    <section class="card" aria-labelledby="s1">
      <h2 id="s1"><span class="n">1</span> Install (2 minutes)</h2>
      <p>First install and log in to at least one agent on the same computer, e.g. Claude Code: <code>claude auth login</code> (or Codex: <code>codex login</code>).</p>
      <p>Try it once without installing (needs Node.js):</p>
      <pre><code>npx t3@latest</code></pre>
      <p>Or install the CLI: <code>curl -fsSL https://t3.codes/install.sh | sh</code>, then run <code>t3</code>. Desktop app: <code>brew install --cask t3-code</code> (macOS), <code>winget install T3Tools.T3Code</code> (Windows), or the .deb / AppImage from GitHub Releases. No <code>t3</code> binary for Intel Macs: use the desktop app there.</p>
      <p class="label"><a href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code">github.com/pingdotgg/t3code</a> · <a href="https://t3.codes">t3.codes</a></p>
    </section>
    <section class="card" aria-labelledby="s2">
      <h2 id="s2"><span class="n">2</span> Start three agents in parallel</h2>
      <p>Add your project (Add project → Local folder), pick a Claude model in the model menu, type the first job and press <code>Cmd+Option+Enter</code>: it sends, keeps that thread running in the background and opens a fresh composer. Type job two, same shortcut; job three, Enter. The sidebar's Working group shows every thread live and flips each to Done.</p>
      <p>Our test: three jobs in a tiny repo (build a weather page, write + run tests, rewrite the README), all three finished about 27 s after the first was sent; 9/9 tests passed; 5 files changed, +260 −2.</p>
      <p>Jobs that touch the same files can collide. For bigger work, pick <strong>New worktree</strong> under the composer so each agent gets its own copy.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card" aria-labelledby="s3">
      <h2 id="s3"><span class="n">3</span> Watch it from your phone</h2>
      <p>Install the T3 Code app (<a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/t3-code-remote-claude-more/id6787819824">iOS</a> / <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.t3tools.t3code">Android</a>), then on the computer run <code>t3 up</code> and choose T3 Connect (free, up to 3 machines) or local network. The phone is a remote: your computer does the work and has to stay on.</p>
      <p><strong>Know before you go:</strong> the app is free; you pay your provider as usual. T3's own FAQ says using Claude through the Agent SDK drains the 5-hour limit faster than Claude Code directly (not the weekly limit). It's "very early", so expect bugs.</p>
      <p class="label"><a href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/blob/main/docs/user/faq.md">docs: FAQ</a> · <a href="https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/blob/main/docs/user/remote-access.md">docs: remote access</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</PackLayout>
